s equivalent to $\\frac{18x-6}{3}?$" 17592186045417] [17592186233078 1072 #uuid "5277b0dd-a1ab-523e-8996-74d7092ca199" 17592186045417] [17592186233078 1074 "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{18x-6}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{18x}{3}-\\frac{6}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{18}{3}\\cdot x-\\frac{6}{3} & = \\\\ 6\\cdot x-2 & = \\\\ 6x-2. & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 17592186045417] [17592186250976 1080 "{6}^{x}ln⁡6-10{x}^{2}+6x" 17592186045417] [17592186250976 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186250976 1083 #uuid "3232bdcf-d781-5e59-bb5b-56c10f0d7fa1" 17592186045417] [17592186251009 1080 "{6}^{x}-10{x}^{2}+6x-19" 17592186045417] [17592186251009 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186251009 1083 #uuid "37865371-b061-54aa-9810-81e59d0b835b" 17592186045417] [17592186251060 1080 "{6}^{x}ln⁡6-10x+6" 17592186045417] [17592186251060 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186251060 1083 #uuid "3d09661f-ce26-5e19-a8b8-2ae50263662e" 17592186045417] [17592186251775 1080 "{6}^{x}-10x+6" 17592186045417] [17592186251775 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186251775 1083 #uuid "9007950f-ce55-5f0c-a1f6-d3963f0294f9" 17592186045417] [17592186252214 1080 "{6}^{x}ln⁡6-10{x}^{2}+6x-19" 17592186045417] [17592186252214 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186252214 1083 #uuid "bbf32e0c-8341-5060-b67e-c44870ab4cd0" 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1075 17592186250976 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1075 17592186251009 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1075 17592186251060 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1075 17592186251775 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1075 17592186252214 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1076 17592186045493 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1077 "selection" 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1078 17592186251060 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1079 #uuid "e849ca6e-9bda-5244-a669-0f22826facaa" 17592186045417] [17592186253334 1068 17592186253210 17592186045417] [17592186253334 1069 "q-11735" 17592186045417] [17592186253334 1070 17592186045485 17592186045417] [17592186253334 1071 "Given that $f(x)={6}^{x}-5{x}^{2}+6x-19$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$" 17592186045417] [17592186253334 1072 #uuid "50678a5c-afcb-522f-98fb-80e9680afca6" 17592186045417] [17592186253334 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x}-5{x}^{2}+6x-19) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(19) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x})-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(19) \\\\  & =ln⁡6\\cdot {6}^{x}-5(2x)+6(1)-0 \\\\  & ={6}^{x}ln⁡6-10x+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 17592186045417] [17592186408166 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox 17592186045416] [17592186409262 1146 17592186251060 17592186045416] [17592186409262 1148 101.998 17592186045443] [17592186409262 1156 17592186409263 17592186045443] [17592186409262 1158 17592186253334 17592186045443] [17592186409262 1161 #uuid "2400d6f0-de9d-4711-a743-56063c38ea56" 17592186045443] [17592186409262 1162 17592186045571 17592186045443] [17592186420504 1068 17592186477605 17592186045436] [17592186420504 1068 17592186477606 17592186045436] [17592186420504 1068 17592186477607 17592186045436] [17592186420504 1069 "q-37456" 17592186045417] [17592186420504 1071 "The function \n$f(x,y)$ \nhas the second derivative\n\n$$\n\\boldsymbol{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nand has a stationary point at $(1,1).$ If $H$ denotes the Hessian determinant of $f,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $H(1,1)>0$\n\nII. $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(1,1)>0$\n\nIII. The point $(1,1)$ is a local minimum of $f$\n\nSelect all that apply." 17592186045443] [17592186420504 1072 #uuid "d1a7556c-36af-5f0b-b64c-a00089e6850e" 17592186045417] [17592186420504 1074 "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ we have the following:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivatives test is inconclusive.\n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the determinant of ${f}^{″}(1,1),$ we get\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=det({f}^{″}(1,1))=2\\cdot 0-{1}^{2}=-1<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(1,1)=({f}^{″}(1,1))_{11}=2>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $H(1,1)<0,$ then $(1,1)$ is a saddle point by the second partial derivative test.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 17592186045443] [17592186477271 1080 "false" 17592186045436] [17592186477271 1082 17592186045499 17592186045436] [17592186477271 1083 #uuid "f54eb3dc-8f1a-5dd1-962f-c6bca73b03cb" 17592186045436] [17592186477272 1080 "true" 17592186045436] [17592186477272 1082 17592186045499 17592186045436] [17592186477272 1083 #uuid "8c3bd524-ddd5-53ed-ac7b-67c5c3c6cc25" 17592186045436] [17592186477273 1080 "false" 17592186045436] [17592186477273 1082 17592186045499 17592186045436] [17592186477273 1083 #uuid "32a85eda-3d96-59fb-ae1a-38073082f1cc" 17592186045436] [17592186477274 1080 "true" 17592186045436] [17592186477274 1082 17592186045499 17592186045436] [17592186477274 1083 #uuid "dc13ebbc-79a8-5f41-b29b-888f990acc60" 17592186045436] [17592186477275 1080 "false" 17592186045436] [17592186477275 1082 17592186045499 17592186045436] [17592186477275 1083 #uuid "3e834f58-d2a9-5c2a-898e-e22835894832" 17592186045436] [17592186477276 1080 "true" 175921